    },
    {
      "text": "atoms (C, N, O, S). The 3D Cartesian coordinates of the most stable conformation and elec-",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        247.91207885742188,
        540.0580444335938,
        258.5282897949219
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "tronic properties (atomization energy, HOMO/LUMO eigenvalues, etc.) of each molecule",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        271.820068359375,
        540.0580444335938,
        282.436279296875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "were determined using ab-initio density functional theory (PBE0/tier2 basis set).17,18 Learn-",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        291.3890686035156,
        540.0040283203125,
        306.3442687988281
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "ing methods benchmarked on QM7/QM7b are responsible for predicting these electronic",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        319.63507080078125,
        540.0460205078125,
        330.25128173828125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "properties given stable conformational coordinates. For the purpose of more stable perfor-",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        343.5430603027344,
        540.070068359375,
        354.1592712402344
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "mances as well as better comparison, we recommend stratiﬁed splitting(introduced in the",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        367.4510498046875,
        540.0339965820312,
        378.0672607421875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "next subsection) for QM7.",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        391.3590393066406,
        206.43624877929688,
        401.9752502441406
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "QM8",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        431.99603271484375,
        101.58911895751953,
        442.61224365234375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The QM8 dataset comes from a recent study on modeling quantum mechanical calculations",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        463.6250305175781,
        540.0579833984375,
        474.2412414550781
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "of electronic spectra and excited state energy of small molecules.42 Multiple methods, in-",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        483.19403076171875,
        539.9992065429688,
        498.14825439453125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "cluding time-dependent density functional theories (TDDFT) and second-order approximate",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        511.4400329589844,
        540.0341796875,
        522.0562744140625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "coupled-cluster (CC2), are applied to a collection of molecules that include up to eight heavy",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        535.3480224609375,
        540.0460815429688,
        545.9642944335938
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "atoms (also a subset of the GDB-17 database43). In total, four excited state properties are",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        557.6826782226562,
        540.0256958007812,
        569.872314453125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "calculated by three diﬀerent methods on 22 thousand samples.",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        583.1640014648438,
        392.578857421875,
        593.7802734375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "QM9",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        623.7999877929688,
        101.58911895751953,
        634.416259765625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "QM9 is a comprehensive dataset that provides geometric, energetic, electronic and ther-",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        655.4290161132812,
        540.0459594726562,
        666.0452880859375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "modynamic properties for a subset of GDB-17 database,43 comprising 134 thousand stable",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        674.9990234375,
        540.0311889648438,
        689.9533081054688
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "organic molecules with up to nine heavy atoms.44 All molecules are modeled using density",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        698.9070434570312,
        540.0086059570312,
        713.861328125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
